# condor_submit_dag sweep_facula_B.dag : the decade at 4096 px (60 rings, hmi.M_45s), noise_th = 8, B_th = 24 G,
# I_th = 0.89, A_th = 20 uHem (plage), T_sp = 500 K, ccf_norm = 2 and the Dumusque bisector times mu
# (settings_facula_B.sh), for the mean field of the faculae B_fc = 50, 100, 200, 250, 300, 500 G: facula intensities
# (1 - B_fc/200) I_quiet + B_fc/200 I_faculae(MURaM 200 G) (parameters_facula_B.txt: noise_th, B_th, I_th, A_th, B_fc,
# Temp), everything in ${BASE}/facula_B:
#   1. the grids of every (Temp, B_fc) (build_grids_facula_B.sub)                                      } at the same time
#   2. identification in 80 blocks of days, the sets of thresholds at once (identify_facula_B.sub)    }
#   3. the days still missing and the filling factors of the set (aggregate_facula_B.sub)
#   4. one simulation per line of parameters_facula_B.txt (run_facula_B.sub)
#   5. table of the RMS against HARPS-N, SORCE, TSIS-1 (collect_facula_B.sub; it runs even if some sets failed)
# Figures: facula_B.ipynb
JOB grids     build_grids_facula_B.sub
JOB ident     identify_facula_B.sub
JOB aggregate aggregate_facula_B.sub
JOB sets      run_facula_B.sub
JOB collect   collect_facula_B.sub
PARENT ident CHILD aggregate
PARENT grids aggregate CHILD sets
PARENT sets  CHILD collect
SCRIPT POST ident /bin/true
SCRIPT POST sets  /bin/true
